{"id": "tea:brhadaranyaka-upanisad-bhasya-sankara:2.3.6", "source": "src:brhadaranyaka-upanisad-bhasya-sankara", "location": {"ref": "2.3.6"}, "paraphrase": "The double negation 'not so, not so' excludes every specification by adjuncts; Brahman cannot be described by name, form, action, distinction, genus or quality, and is indicated only by negation.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "apophatic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["ultimate"], "terms": ["trm:neti-neti"], "concepts": ["cpt:neti-neti"], "practices": ["prc:neti-neti"], "teachers": ["tch:sankara"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U13-advaita"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U13-advaita"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:brhadaranyaka-upanisad-bhasya-sankara:4.4.22", "source": "src:brhadaranyaka-upanisad-bhasya-sankara", "location": {"ref": "4.4.22"}, "paraphrase": "The text's 'desiring this world (the self) alone, renunciants wander forth' enjoins renunciation; sacrifice, gifts and austerity produce the desire to know (vividiṣā), and the knower renounces all works.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge", "action"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["practice", "ethics"], "concepts": ["cpt:sannyasa-advaita", "cpt:karma-in-advaita"], "practices": ["prc:vividisa-sannyasa", "prc:vidvat-sannyasa"], "terms": ["trm:vividisa"], "disputes": ["dsp:jnana-karma-samuccaya"], "cross_refs": ["tea:brhadaranyaka-upanisad:4.4.22"], "teachers": ["tch:sankara"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U13-advaita"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U13-advaita"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:brhadaranyaka-upanisad-bhasya-sankara:5.1.1", "source": "src:brhadaranyaka-upanisad-bhasya-sankara", "location": {"ref": "5.1.1"}, "paraphrase": "Against the view that knowledge must be combined with works and that the world is really both one and many (difference-in-identity), Śaṅkara argues that difference and non-difference cannot both be real of one thing.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "polemical", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["dispute"], "teachers": ["tch:sankara", "tch:bhartrprapanca"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "disputes": ["dsp:jnana-karma-samuccaya", "dsp:world-real-or-appearance"], "notes": "Bhartṛprapañca's views are refuted at several places in the commentary (the opponent is named by Ānandagiri); the specific locator 5.1.1 (pūrṇam adaḥ) is given with low confidence.", "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U13-advaita"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U13-advaita"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
